<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/16th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chichimeca War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1550–<a href="/years/1590">1590</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chichimeca">Chichimeca</a> War was a long conflict between Spanish colonists and the nomadic and semi-nomadic peoples of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a> known collectively as Chichimecas. Sparked by the opening of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zacatecas">Zacatecas</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">silver</a> mines, it centred on raids along the road between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico-city">Mexico City</a> and the mines. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> ended it around 1590 less by force than by a policy of food and goods, settlements of allied <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tlaxcalans">Tlaxcalans</a> and missions.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/chichimeca-war.jpg" alt="Chichimeca War" width="320" height="352" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Juan Carlos Fonseca Mata · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mapa_de_San_Miguel_y_San_Felipe_de_los_Chichimecas_(1580)_-_Chichimecas_1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
